{"id": "haiku__GEN__omni_405__9", "result": "$x^2 - y^2 = (x-y)(x+y)$.\n\nLet $a = 2001^{1002}$, so $a^{-1} = 2001^{-1002}$.\n\n- $x - y = (a - a^{-1}) - (a + a^{-1}) = -2a^{-1}$\n- $x + y = (a - a^{-1}) + (a + a^{-1}) = 2a$\n\nSo $x^2 - y^2 = (-2a^{-1})(2a) = -4$.\n\nCheck by expanding: $x^2 = a^2 - 2 + a^{-2}$ and $y^2 = a^2 + 2 + a^{-2}$, so $x^2 - y^2 = -4$.\n\nANSWER: -4", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.0003487900000000001, "model_used": ["claude-haiku-5-5"], "secs": 5.1}